<!--Post: 8342--><!--Time: 1109079345-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8342"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 5:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found it interesting that Ted Bundy started his killing sprees within a month of the Otero murders. See Timeline: <a href="http://tedbundy.150m.com/list2.html" target=_top>http://tedbundy.150m.com/list2.html</a> <BR> <BR>His very last murders in Florida were on 1/15/78, the date 1/15 of the Otero murders. The two poems by BTK were sent within weeks of Bundy&#39;s capture in 1978.  <BR> <BR>The Nancy Fox poem was sent by BTK on the date of Bundy&#39;s last murder on 2/9/78. Victim, 12 year old Kimberly Leach, close to the age of Josephine Otero. <BR> <BR>Also compare the pictures of the young Shirley and Kimberly Leach. They vaguely resemble each other. Scroll down for the picture of Kimberly on the following website: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/notorious/bundy/run_9.html?sect=" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/notorio us/bundy/run_9.html?sect=</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/news.html" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/news.html</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8342-->
<!--Post: 8359--><!--Time: 1109091504-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8359"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 8:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, you are right. the resemblance is eerie.  <BR> <BR>It is also thought that Ted might have been responsible for the deaths of young girls, 9 or so, when he was around that age as well. No one will ever know now. I wonder if BTK and Bundy ever crossed paths. Water seeks its own level. Recognizing a kindred spirit can often take place without a word being spoken. Eyes meet across the room, and voila. <BR> <BR>Does BTK think of Ted&#39;s not so infamous end? Perhaps one day another woman will step forward and light up &#39;Old Sparky&#39; and BTK will be in the chair. Bundy wasn&#39;t quite as smug before he died. People that were with him stated that he was nervous.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8359-->
<!--Post: 8445--><!--Time: 1109133347-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8445"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 8:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Teardrop, <BR>Bundy was in custody when Son of Sam was caught by the Taskforce Omega on August 10, 1977. When Bundy escaped, he went to Florida and killed girls from the Chi Omega Sorority. A coincidence or are these serial killers keeping tabs on each other? Son of Sam&#39;s father lived in Florida at the time too. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8445-->
<!--Post: 8474--><!--Time: 1109169309-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8474"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 6:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I can believe that the more intelligent ones may do just that. BTK does show insight into his condition, as it were, though he voices frustration about not being able to get help. BTK does plan to go down in history, so he needs to keep an eye on the competition. And pickup pointers.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8474-->
<!--Post: 8640--><!--Time: 1109260114-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8640"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 7:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop,about his insight, perhaps he uses the &#34;monster inside&#34; quip to justify  his actions when and if he is caught.  An insanity defense would be a hard sell but maybe he is planning ahead.  Serial killers are known to admire and keep tabs on one another. I believe they compare, envy and learn from one another. Several of them who have been sentenced correspond with each other on a regular basis.  Remember the interest and &#34;help&#34; Bundy gave with the Green River Task Force?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8640-->
<!--Post: 8699--><!--Time: 1109292711-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8699"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 4:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I would imagine that before BTK is apprehended that we ought to get used to the idea that he will be &#34;institutionalized&#34; for the rest of his natural life and be happy to be rid of him. <BR> <BR>Between jurisdictional disputes, psychiatric tests, appeals, I don&#39;t expect a speedy trial. <BR> <BR>But...that does bring up an interesting point. Part of his M.O. is that he invades the home of the victim, and as far as I know, there has not been any solid link to any victims that were found outside the home. <BR> <BR>Is it possible that he is trying to keep the investigation focused locally by avoiding any &#34;kidnapping charges&#34; which would automatically give the FBI jurisdiction. I noticed some &#34;inferred&#34; and &#34;unsubstanciated&#34; evidence that he wants to keep the whole thing very much &#34;Wichita and BTK&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8699-->
<!--Post: 8804--><!--Time: 1109351953-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8804"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 9:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;the monster inside&#34; <BR>Son of Sam had demons telling him what to do. <BR> <BR>I forgot what show I was watching, but there was a suggestion that it would be better to study these serial killers rather than put them to death.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8804-->
<!--Post: 9100--><!--Time: 1109394788-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9100"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 9:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bookworm ideally that would be a great idea but because serial killers et al are so manipulative it would be impossible to study them,  About the only thing constant about them is there manipulation and self pity.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9100-->
<!--Post: 9104--><!--Time: 1109394998-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9104"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 9:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bookworm:  I believe Dahmer was the exception.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
